IMPORT prelude

-- Interpretation Act 1987 (New South Wales), Part 8 Statutory bodies: sections 50 to 53A. Section 51 is printed "(Repealed)".
-- Whether a thing is a statutory corporation, or a person is qualified, is a plain input.

§ `Part 8 Statutory bodies`

§§ `50 Statutory corporations`

-- What section 50(1) says a statutory corporation has or may do.
DECLARE CapacityOfAStatutoryCorporation IS ONE OF
    PerpetualSuccession
    ASeal
    TakingProceedingsAndBeingProceededAgainstInItsCorporateName
    DealingWithPropertyToEnableItToExerciseItsFunctions
    DoingAndSufferingOtherThingsThatBodiesCorporateMayDoAndSufferAndAreNecessaryOrIncidental
    SomeOtherCapacityOfAStatutoryCorporation

-- src:570 | (1) A statutory corporation—
-- src:571 | (a) has perpetual succession,
-- src:572 | (b) shall have a seal,
-- src:573 | (c) may take proceedings and be proceeded against in its corporate name,
-- src:574 | (d) may, for the purpose of enabling it to exercise its functions, purchase, exchange, take on lease, hold, dispose of and otherwise deal with property, and
-- src:575 | (e) may do and suffer all other things that bodies corporate may, by law, do and suffer and that are necessary for, or incidental to, the exercise of its functions.
@ref s 50(1) (src:570-575)
GIVEN `it is a statutory corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      capacity IS A CapacityOfAStatutoryCorporation
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 50(1) a statutory corporation has the capacity` MEANS
    IF `it is a statutory corporation`
    THEN CONSIDER capacity
         WHEN PerpetualSuccession THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN ASeal THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN TakingProceedingsAndBeingProceededAgainstInItsCorporateName THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN DealingWithPropertyToEnableItToExerciseItsFunctions THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN DoingAndSufferingOtherThingsThatBodiesCorporateMayDoAndSufferAndAreNecessaryOrIncidental THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN SomeOtherCapacityOfAStatutoryCorporation THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:576 | (2) The seal of a statutory corporation (being a corporation that has 2 or more members) shall be kept by the president, chairperson or other principal officer of the corporation and shall be affixed to a document only—
@ref s 50(2) custody (src:576)
GIVEN `the corporation has 2 or more members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seal is kept by the president, chairperson or other principal officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 50(2) the seal of the statutory corporation is kept as the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the corporation has 2 or more members` THEN JUST `the seal is kept by the president, chairperson or other principal officer of the corporation` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:576 | (2) The seal of a statutory corporation (being a corporation that has 2 or more members) shall be kept by the president, chairperson or other principal officer of the corporation and shall be affixed to a document only—
-- src:577 | (a) in the presence of at least 2 members of the corporation, and
-- src:578 | (b) with an attestation by the signatures of those members of the fact of the affixing of the seal.
@ref s 50(2) affixing (src:576-578)
GIVEN `the corporation has 2 or more members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seal is affixed in the presence of at least 2 members of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affixing is attested by the signatures of those members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 50(2) the seal is affixed to the document` MEANS
    IF `the corporation has 2 or more members` AND (NOT (`the seal is affixed in the presence of at least 2 members of the corporation` AND `the affixing is attested by the signatures of those members`))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:579 | (3) Every document requiring authentication by a statutory corporation may be sufficiently authenticated without the seal of the corporation—
-- src:580 | (a) in the case of a corporation that has 2 or more members—if it is signed by the president, chairperson or other principal officer of the corporation or by any member of the staff of the corporation authorised to do so by the president, chairperson or other principal officer,
-- src:581 | (b) in the case of a corporation sole—if it is signed by the person by whom the corporation is constituted or by any member of the staff of the corporation authorised to do so by that person, or
-- src:582 | (c) in the case of a corporation that has no members—if it is signed by the person for the time being managing the affairs of the corporation or by any member of the staff of the corporation authorised to do so by that person.
@ref s 50(3) (src:579-582)
GIVEN `the document is signed by the person the paragraph names for the corporation, that is the president, chairperson or other principal officer where the corporation has 2 or more members, the person by whom the corporation is constituted where it is a corporation sole, or the person for the time being managing its affairs where it has no members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is signed by a member of the staff of the corporation authorised to do so by that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 50(3) the document requiring authentication is sufficiently authenticated without the seal of the corporation` MEANS
    IF `the document is signed by the person the paragraph names for the corporation, that is the president, chairperson or other principal officer where the corporation has 2 or more members, the person by whom the corporation is constituted where it is a corporation sole, or the person for the time being managing its affairs where it has no members` OR `the document is signed by a member of the staff of the corporation authorised to do so by that person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:583 | (4) This section applies to a statutory corporation in addition to, and without limiting the effect of, any provision of the Act by or under which the corporation is constituted.
@ref s 50(4) (src:583)
GIVEN `it is a statutory corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 50(4) section 50 applies to the statutory corporation in addition to any provision of the Act by or under which the corporation is constituted` MEANS
    IF `it is a statutory corporation` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `52 Proceedings of statutory bodies`

-- The matters section 52(1) says an act or proceeding of a statutory body is not called into question for.
DECLARE MatterAboutAStatutoryBody IS ONE OF
    VacanciesInTheMembershipOfTheBody
    FaultsInTheAppointmentOfAnyMembersOfTheBody
    DisqualificationsOfAnyMembersOfTheBody
    MinorIrregularitiesInTheMannerInWhichMeetingsHaveBeenConvenedOrConducted
    ThePresenceOrParticipationAtMeetingsOfPersonsNotEntitledToBePresentOrToParticipate
    SomeOtherMatterAboutAStatutoryBody

-- src:588 | (1) Any act or proceeding of a statutory body shall not be called into question merely because of—
-- src:589 | (a) any vacancies in the membership of the body,
-- src:590 | (b) any defects in the appointment of any members of the body,
-- src:591 | (c) any disqualifications of any members of the body,
-- src:592 | (d) any minor irregularities in the manner in which any meetings of the body have been convened or conducted, or
-- src:593 | (e) the presence or participation at any meetings of the body of any persons not entitled to be present or to participate at those meetings.
@ref s 52(1) (src:588-593)
GIVEN matter IS A MatterAboutAStatutoryBody
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52(1) an act or proceeding of a statutory body is called into question merely because of the matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN VacanciesInTheMembershipOfTheBody THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN FaultsInTheAppointmentOfAnyMembersOfTheBody THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN DisqualificationsOfAnyMembersOfTheBody THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN MinorIrregularitiesInTheMannerInWhichMeetingsHaveBeenConvenedOrConducted THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN ThePresenceOrParticipationAtMeetingsOfPersonsNotEntitledToBePresentOrToParticipate THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN SomeOtherMatterAboutAStatutoryBody THEN NOTHING

-- src:594 | (2) This section applies to a statutory body in addition to, and without limiting the effect of, any provision of the Act by or under which the body is constituted.
@ref s 52(2) (src:594)
GIVEN `it is a statutory body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52(2) section 52 applies to the statutory body in addition to any provision of the Act by or under which the body is constituted` MEANS
    IF `it is a statutory body` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `53 Alterations of names and constitutions`

-- src:597 | (1) If an Act or statutory rule alters the name of a body or office—
-- src:598 | (a) the body or office continues in existence under its new name so that its identity is not affected, and
@ref s 53(1)(a) (src:597-598)
GIVEN `an Act or statutory rule alters the name of a body or office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 53(1)(a) the body or office continues in existence under its new name so that its identity is not affected` MEANS
    IF `an Act or statutory rule alters the name of a body or office` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:597 | (1) If an Act or statutory rule alters the name of a body or office—
-- src:598 | (a) the body or office continues in existence under its new name so that its identity is not affected, and
-- src:599 | (b) a reference in any Act or instrument, or in any other document, to the body or office under its former name shall, except in relation to matters that occurred before the alteration took place, be read as a reference to the body or office under its new name.
@ref s 53(1)(b) (src:597-599)
GIVEN `an Act or statutory rule alters the name of a body or office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference is to matters that occurred before the alteration took place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 53(1)(b) a reference to the body or office under its former name is read as a reference to the body or office under its new name` MEANS
    IF `an Act or statutory rule alters the name of a body or office` THEN JUST (NOT `the reference is to matters that occurred before the alteration took place`) ELSE JUST FALSE

-- What section 53(2) says an alteration of a body's constitution does not affect.
DECLARE ThingUnaffectedByAnAlterationOfConstitution IS ONE OF
    TheIdentityOfTheBody
    TheFunctionsOfTheBody
    LegalOrOtherProceedingsInstitutedOrToBeInstitutedByOrAgainstTheBody
    AnInvestigationOrInquiryByAnotherPersonOrBodyIntoActionTakenOrPracticeEngagedInByTheBody
    SomeOtherThingAboutTheBody

-- src:600 | (2) If an Act or statutory rule alters the constitution of a body—
-- src:601 | (a) the body continues in existence as newly constituted so that its identity is not affected,
-- src:602 | (b) the alteration does not affect any functions of the body,
-- src:603 | (c) the alteration does not affect any legal or other proceedings instituted or to be instituted by or against the body and any legal or other proceedings that might have been continued or commenced by or against the body as previously constituted may be continued or commenced by or against the body as newly constituted, and
-- src:604 | (d) the alteration does not affect any investigation or inquiry being or proposed to be undertaken by any other person or body into any action taken or practice engaged in by the body before the alteration took place and any investigation or inquiry that might have been continued or commenced into any such action or practice may be continued or commenced as if the action had been taken or the practice had been engaged in by the body as newly constituted.
@ref s 53(2) (src:600-604)
GIVEN `an Act or statutory rule alters the constitution of a body` IS A BOOLEAN
      thing IS A ThingUnaffectedByAnAlterationOfConstitution
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 53(2) the alteration of the constitution of the body affects the thing` MEANS
    IF `an Act or statutory rule alters the constitution of a body`
    THEN CONSIDER thing
         WHEN TheIdentityOfTheBody THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN TheFunctionsOfTheBody THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN LegalOrOtherProceedingsInstitutedOrToBeInstitutedByOrAgainstTheBody THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN AnInvestigationOrInquiryByAnotherPersonOrBodyIntoActionTakenOrPracticeEngagedInByTheBody THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN SomeOtherThingAboutTheBody THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:603 | (c) the alteration does not affect any legal or other proceedings instituted or to be instituted by or against the body and any legal or other proceedings that might have been continued or commenced by or against the body as previously constituted may be continued or commenced by or against the body as newly constituted, and
@ref s 53(2)(c) continuation (src:603)
GIVEN `an Act or statutory rule alters the constitution of a body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings might have been continued or commenced by or against the body as previously constituted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 53(2)(c) the proceedings may be continued or commenced by or against the body as newly constituted` MEANS
    IF `an Act or statutory rule alters the constitution of a body` AND `the proceedings might have been continued or commenced by or against the body as previously constituted` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:604 | (d) the alteration does not affect any investigation or inquiry being or proposed to be undertaken by any other person or body into any action taken or practice engaged in by the body before the alteration took place and any investigation or inquiry that might have been continued or commenced into any such action or practice may be continued or commenced as if the action had been taken or the practice had been engaged in by the body as newly constituted.
@ref s 53(2)(d) continuation (src:604)
GIVEN `an Act or statutory rule alters the constitution of a body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the investigation or inquiry might have been continued or commenced into the action or practice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 53(2)(d) the investigation or inquiry may be continued or commenced as if the action had been taken or the practice had been engaged in by the body as newly constituted` MEANS
    IF `an Act or statutory rule alters the constitution of a body` AND `the investigation or inquiry might have been continued or commenced into the action or practice` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `53A Extension of age limit for part-time members of statutory bodies`

-- src:607 | (1) If—
-- src:608 | (a) a person is or has, within the last 3 months, been the holder of a part-time office as a member of a statutory body,
-- src:609 | (b) the person cannot be re-appointed to the office because a provision of an Act or statutory rule imposes an age limit,
-- src:610 | (c) a Minister certifies to the Governor that that Minister is of the opinion that it is in the public interest that the person should be able to continue to hold the office after reaching the age limit, and
-- src:611 | (d) the person has reached the age limit or is within 3 months of reaching it,
-- src:612 | the Governor may extend the age limit for the person, but not beyond the age of 72 years.
@ref s 53A(1) (src:607-612)
GIVEN `the person is or has, within the last 3 months, been the holder of a part-time office as a member of a statutory body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person cannot be re-appointed to the office because a provision of an Act or statutory rule imposes an age limit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a Minister certifies to the Governor that that Minister is of the opinion that it is in the public interest that the person should be able to continue to hold the office after reaching the age limit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has reached the age limit or is within 3 months of reaching it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposed extended age limit in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 53A(1) the Governor may extend the age limit for the person` MEANS
    IF     `the person is or has, within the last 3 months, been the holder of a part-time office as a member of a statutory body`
       AND `the person cannot be re-appointed to the office because a provision of an Act or statutory rule imposes an age limit`
       AND `a Minister certifies to the Governor that that Minister is of the opinion that it is in the public interest that the person should be able to continue to hold the office after reaching the age limit`
       AND `the person has reached the age limit or is within 3 months of reaching it`
    THEN JUST (`the proposed extended age limit in years` AT MOST 72)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:613 | (2) While under the extended age limit, the person (if otherwise qualified) may be re-appointed to the office.
@ref s 53A(2) (src:613)
GIVEN `the person is under the extended age limit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is otherwise qualified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 53A(2) the person may be re-appointed to the office` MEANS
    IF `the person is under the extended age limit` AND `the person is otherwise qualified` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:614 | (3) An office held by a person re-appointed under this section becomes vacant if the person reaches the extended age limit, instead of the former age limit.
@ref s 53A(3) (src:614)
GIVEN `the person has been re-appointed under section 53A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person reaches the extended age limit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 53A(3) the office becomes vacant` MEANS
    IF `the person has been re-appointed under section 53A` AND `the person reaches the extended age limit` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:615 | (4) This section prevails over any Act or statutory rule relating to the constitution of the statutory body concerned, unless any such Act or statutory rule expressly excludes this section.
@ref s 53A(4) (src:615)
GIVEN `an Act or statutory rule relating to the constitution of the statutory body expressly excludes section 53A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 53A(4) section 53A prevails over the Act or statutory rule relating to the constitution of the statutory body` MEANS
    IF `an Act or statutory rule relating to the constitution of the statutory body expressly excludes section 53A` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:616 | (5) A notification in the Gazette by a Minister to the effect that the age limit has been extended for the person is evidence of the extension.
@ref s 53A(5) (src:616)
GIVEN `it is a notification in the Gazette by a Minister to the effect that the age limit has been extended for the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 53A(5) the notification is evidence of the extension` MEANS
    IF `it is a notification in the Gazette by a Minister to the effect that the age limit has been extended for the person` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:617 | (6) The age limit for a person may be extended under this section on more than one occasion, but so that the age limit is not extended beyond the age of 72 years.
@ref s 53A(6) (src:617)
GIVEN `the age limit for the person has been extended under section 53A on an earlier occasion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposed extended age limit in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 53A(6) the age limit for the person may be extended on a further occasion` MEANS
    IF `the age limit for the person has been extended under section 53A on an earlier occasion` THEN JUST (`the proposed extended age limit in years` AT MOST 72) ELSE NOTHING

-- src:618 | (7) In this section, part-time office means an office other than—
-- src:619 | (a) an office required to be held on a full-time basis, or
-- src:620 | (b) an office specified in any of the Schedules to the Statutory and Other Offices Remuneration Act 1975.
@ref s 53A(7) (src:618-620)
GIVEN `the office is required to be held on a full-time basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the office is specified in a Schedule to the Statutory and Other Offices Remuneration Act 1975` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 53A(7) the office is a part-time office` MEANS
    (NOT `the office is required to be held on a full-time basis`) AND (NOT `the office is specified in a Schedule to the Statutory and Other Offices Remuneration Act 1975`)

